<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xmile version="1.0" xmlns="http://docs.oasis-open.org/xmile/ns/XMILE/v1.0">
    <!--
    PROBE for Stella: does Stella support a variable declared over the same
    dimension twice?

    The XMILE v1.0 spec (section 4.5.2) itself gives a non-apply-to-all
    example declared "X by X, where X is size 2", so the spec sanctions the
    shape by example. Vensim DSS rejects the equivalent declaration outright
    ("DimA appears more than once on LHS", measured 2026-08-04). Stella is the
    tiebreaker.

    sq is declared [X, X] with sq[i,j] = 10*i + j, so every cell is distinct:
    11,12,13 / 21,22,23 / 31,32,33.

    Please open in Stella, run, and report:
      - whether Stella accepts the model at all (an error naming sq or the
        double dimension is itself the answer);
      - the values of probe_copy, probe_row, and probe_sum.

    Prediction table:
      - Stella REJECTS the declaration: matches Vensim; the spec example is a
        dead letter in both major tools.
      - probe_copy = 11,12,13,21,22,23,31,32,33 with probe_row = 36,66,96 and
        probe_sum = 198: a true 2-D array, the plain spec reading.
      - probe_copy = 11,11,11,22,22,22,33,33,33 or probe_sum = 66: some
        diagonal/first-axis rule (Simlin today reads the first axis for both
        subscripts, which is measured, disclosed behavior with no external
        referent so far).
    -->
    <header>
        <vendor>Simlin</vendor>
        <name>stella repeated dimension probe</name>
        <product version="0.1.0">Simlin</product>
    </header>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="months">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>1</stop>
        <dt>1</dt>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="X" size="3"/>
    </dimensions>
    <model>
        <variables>
            <aux name="sq">
                <dimensions>
                    <dim name="X"/>
                    <dim name="X"/>
                </dimensions>
                <element subscript="1,1"><eqn>11</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="1,2"><eqn>12</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="1,3"><eqn>13</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="2,1"><eqn>21</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="2,2"><eqn>22</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="2,3"><eqn>23</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="3,1"><eqn>31</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="3,2"><eqn>32</eqn></element>
                <element subscript="3,3"><eqn>33</eqn></element>
            </aux>
            <aux name="probe_copy">
                <dimensions>
                    <dim name="X"/>
                    <dim name="X"/>
                </dimensions>
                <eqn>sq[X, X]</eqn>
            </aux>
            <aux name="probe_row">
                <dimensions>
                    <dim name="X"/>
                </dimensions>
                <eqn>SUM(sq[X, *])</eqn>
            </aux>
            <aux name="probe_sum">
                <eqn>SUM(sq[*, *])</eqn>
            </aux>
        </variables>
        <views>
            <view type="stock_flow">
                <aux name="sq" x="120" y="120"/>
                <aux name="probe_copy" x="280" y="80"/>
                <aux name="probe_row" x="280" y="160"/>
                <aux name="probe_sum" x="280" y="240"/>
            </view>
        </views>
    </model>
</xmile>
